    "connexions.adminConsentStepsSummary": "Does your administrator want the exact steps?",
    "connexions.adminConsentStep1": "They open the link above, signed in with their Microsoft 365 administrator account (not yours).",
    "connexions.adminConsentStep2": "Microsoft shows “Meet Aaron” with the requested permissions and the verified domain meetaaron.app.",
    "connexions.adminConsentStep3": "They tick “Consent on behalf of your organization” and accept.",
    "connexions.adminConsentStep4": "You come back to this page and click “Connect”: it works, for you and your colleagues.",
    "connexions.adminConsentVerifiedOnly": "If your company only allows “verified publishers”: that setting only blocks employee consent, never the administrator’s. So the link above is still the right answer — nothing needs to be turned off in the tenant.",
    "connexions.adminConsentRevoke": "At any time the administrator can undo it: Microsoft Entra → Enterprise applications → Meet Aaron → Delete. Access stops immediately.",
    "connexions.oauthErrorBanner.admin_consent_required": "Your company (Microsoft 365) requires an administrator's approval before an app can access your mailbox. You can't do this yourself: send this link to whoever manages IT — one approval covers the whole company.",
    "connexions.adminConsentCopy": "Copy the message for the administrator",
    "connexions.adminConsentCopied": "Copied ✓",
    "connexions.adminConsentOpen": "I'm the administrator — authorise now",
    "connexions.adminConsentMessage": "Hello, I use Meet Aaron (meetaaron.app) for my sales prospecting. The app needs access to my Outlook mailbox and calendar to write to my prospects on my behalf and book meetings. Microsoft 365 requires your administrator approval. Could you open this link and approve? It takes a minute and covers every account in the company:",
    "connexions.adminConsentHint": "The administrator approves exactly the same access you would have approved yourself: read and send email on your behalf, and manage your calendar. Once approved, come back here and click “Connect”.",
    "connexions.adminConsentGranted": "All set: your administrator has authorised Meet Aaron for the whole company. Now click “Connect” to link your mailbox.",
    "connexions.adminConsentRefused": "The authorisation wasn't granted. Without it, Microsoft 365 blocks Aaron from accessing your mailbox — talk to your administrator again, or connect a Gmail address in the meantime.",
